# ---- Other people's material: on the bench PC, never committed (added for the public repository) ------------
# Vendor datasheets, manuals, schematics and product photos.
/datasheets/
# TUL's board files for the PYNQ-Z2 and its product photo.  gateware/build.tcl looks for them in
# gateware/board_files/pynq-z2/A.0/ (gateware/README.md says where they come from).
/gateware/board_files/
# JLCPCB's and EasyEDA's land patterns, cached by mfg/footprint_check.py: theirs, and fetched again when stale.
/mfg/jlc_footprint_cache.json
# the phone's originals of photos/ are in build/photos_revA/ (build/ is ignored below)

# ---- Tools' droppings
__pycache__/
*.pyc
fp-info-cache
*-backups
*.lck
.history/
.DS_Store
# working notes exchanged with Claude
/QUESTIONS.md
/ANSWERS.md

# Everything build.py regenerates.  Its header says "Everything below is
# REGENERATED", and `python3 build.py --clean` deletes exactly this.  A clean
# rebuild reproduces every fab output byte for byte (the board file itself
# differs only in uuids that pcbnew rewrites as it pours the zones -- see
# build.py's docstring, which has the measurement).
build/

# Vivado's PS7 board-preset automation writes a summary into a directory named
# from an unset variable, next to wherever it was launched.  Noise, not output.
NA/

# JLCPCB API responses: 5 MB, re-fetched on demand, and every entry is stamped
# with the time of its own query so it goes stale by design.  The pricing that
# matters is already baked into mfg/release/annotated_bom.md.
mfg/jlc_cache.json

# Pre-rewrite snapshots of the placer sources.  The three that existed were
# byte-identical to commit b40dae4, so they were deleted rather than tracked;
# `git show b40dae4:GPSDO-PYNQ-Z2/pcb/<file>.py` is the recovery.  The rule
# stays as insurance in case something makes more of them.
*.r14

# gateware/ has its own .gitignore for the Vivado project and build tree.

# Ad-hoc kicad-cli reports written next to the board rather than into build/.
# build.py puts its own DRC and ERC in build/ on every run; these are whatever
# was left behind by a one-off command or by the GUI, they carry no date in
# their name, and the ones sitting here in round 36 were from 2026-09-13 --
# eight rounds stale and describing a board that no longer exists.  A stale
# report that looks current is worse than no report.
/*-drc.rpt
/*-erc.rpt
/filled-drc.rpt

# Attachments generated FOR an LLM design review: board renders, sheet PDFs,
# DRC dumps and a zone-filled copy of the board.  14 MB, all of it derived
# from whatever the board was on the day, and design_review/Gemini3.8Flash/
# and design_review/Grok4.6/ set the pattern -- the review's MARKDOWN is
# tracked, and so is any code written by hand for it, but not the renders.
design_review/*/*.png
design_review/*/*.pdf
design_review/*/drc-*.json
design_review/*/filled.kicad_p*

# The netlist the release scripts export and re-read every run (mfg/bomdata.py).
# KiCad writes the schematic's ABSOLUTE path into it, and nothing committed may
# name /home (2026-10-09: it had been tracked since rev A).
mfg/_netlist.net
